  "_comment": "The kitchen menu per era. build.mjs INLINES this as const MENUS - never fetched at runtime (CSP, file:// CORS). Edit here, then run: node build.mjs",
  "_rules": "bins is exactly 12 slots (null = empty), and a bin NEVER MOVES: a key set in era N must sit at the same index in every later era; a later era may only fill a slot that was null. plate <= 7 characters (a 44px plate). ticket <= 12 characters (the 72px ticket line). short is the NOW BUILDING readout: 12 x chars + 9 x steps <= 127, steps = recipe length including the base. recipe is [base, ingredient...]: 2..7 keys, base first and only first, then bins of that era. price is integer cents and is flavour only. build.mjs rejects all of it, loudly.",
  "_keys": "Bin and base keys are what the lattice art in content/lattice/ is named for: BEEF BEANS LETTUCE TOMATO ONION CCQ PEPPERS CREAM CHEESE SAUCE CHILI CHICKEN, bases SMALL SHELL LARGE CHIPS. Do not rename a key without renaming its art.",
  "_drops": "Where a real Taco Shop item lists an ingredient with no bin (Monterey Jack, olives, green onions, rice, the whole-wheat tortilla), it is dropped from the recipe and noted on the item. Items whose base comes mid-build (Loco Taco, Taco Supreme) and items needing a second tortilla (3 Amigos, Borracho, Mexican Pizza) or a bun (Taco Burger) are left out: ingredient 0 is always the base."
}
